TI  - Trails Revisited: Associative Indexing in Personal Knowledge Tools Eighty Years After the Memex
AU  - Marchetti, Elisa
T2  - Proceedings of the 35th ACM Conference on Hypertext and Social Media
T3  - HT '24
SP  - 201
EP  - 210
PY  - 2024
DA  - 2026/08/26/
PB  - ACM
CY  - Poznan, Poland
AB  - Bush's memex proposed that a reader could tie two items together and later replay the chain of associations as a trail. Contemporary personal knowledge tools implement links and backlinks but rarely trails: ordered, named, shareable paths through material. We analyze 18 tools and find that 16 support bidirectional links, 5 support ordered sequences, and none preserves the reason a connection was made. We argue the reason, not the link, was the memex's central idea.
