TI  - Where Did That Idea Come From? Provenance Trails in Researchers' Note-Taking
AU  - Halvorsen, Tor
AU  - Quist, Amara
T2  - Proceedings of the ACM on Human-Computer Interaction
VL  - 9
IS  - CSCW2
SP  - 1
EP  - 24
PY  - 2025
DA  - 2026/09/02/
AB  - Researchers write notes across many tools and later struggle to recall where an idea came from. In a three-week diary study with 19 researchers, we asked participants to trace the origin of a sample of their own notes. After two weeks, 31% of notes had no recoverable source; most of these originated in conversations, chat with AI assistants, or reading that was not saved. Participants valued provenance most when writing related work and when revisiting abandoned projects.
